# Placeholder GUIDs are empty (R6)

The workspace handles many GUID-shaped fields: `agent_uuid`,
`tenant_guid`, `machine_guid`, `enrollment_token_id`, per-tenant
enrollment defaults. The audit found **five** different spellings of
"not configured" in active use — `""`, `"0"`, the zero GUID, the
zero-plus-one GUID, and the sequence GUID
`12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012` — producing five different
downstream behaviors: a `WHERE tenant_guid = '0'` that matched nothing,
an enrollment that sent the zero GUID and got a confusing `404 tenant
not found`, and an Event Log entry showing the sequence GUID that looked
like real machine data to the SIEM team.

## The rule

> **The sentinel "not yet configured" for any GUID-shaped field in this
> workspace is the empty string. Never `"0"`, never
> `"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"`, never
> `"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"`, never
> `"12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012"`, never any other placeholder
> GUID value. Validators check `String::is_empty()` (or
> `Option::None` if the type is `Option<Uuid>`).**

Crates with legacy magic-GUID values still on disk provide the one-shot
migration helper below, collapsing every known magic value to empty
(or `None`) on first load.

## Required validation pattern

```rust
fn validate_agent_uuid(s: &str) -> Result<(), Validation> {
    if s.is_empty() {
        return Err(Validation::NotConfigured("AGENT_UUID"));
    }
    Uuid::parse_str(s).map_err(|e| Validation::Malformed { key: "AGENT_UUID", source: e })?;
    Ok(())
}
```

`is_empty()` is the ONLY sentinel check — no `s == "12345678-…"` branch,
no `Uuid::nil() == parsed` branch. Post-migration, a surviving magic
GUID parses as a real GUID and downstream code reports a clear "no
tenant with that GUID exists", which is the correct behavior.

## Required one-shot migration helper

```rust
/// Returns Some(normalized) if `raw` is a known magic-GUID placeholder;
/// None if `raw` is already empty or a genuine GUID-shaped value.
pub fn normalize_legacy_guid_sentinel(raw: &str) -> Option<String> {
    const SENTINELS: &[&str] = &[
        "0",
        "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
        "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
        "12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012",
    ];
    SENTINELS.iter().any(|s| s.eq_ignore_ascii_case(raw)).then(String::new)
}
```

Called once per crate in the startup migration path (R3):

```rust
for key in ["AGENT_UUID", "DEFAULT_TENANT_GUID", "MACHINE_GUID"] {
    if let Some(raw) = cfg.raw_value(key)? {
        if let Some(normalized) = normalize_legacy_guid_sentinel(&raw) {
            tracing::info!(%key, %raw, "collapsing legacy magic-GUID placeholder to empty");
            cfg.set_value(key, &normalized)?;   // R2 manifest gate still applies
        }
    }
}
```

## Forbidden constructs

- `const DEFAULT_TENANT_GUID: &str = "12345678-…";` or any literal
  sequence GUID used as a sentinel.
- Literal zero / zero-plus-one GUIDs used as sentinels. (A documented
  vendor-reserved zero GUID in an external protocol is exempt — add a
  per-site `#[allow]` and a comment.)
- `if guid == "0" { … treat as not set … }` — both the comparison string
  and the practice.
- `Default::default()` on a `Uuid` field the surrounding type later
  treats as "not set" — that silently produces the zero GUID. Use
  `Option<Uuid>` / `None`, or `String` / `""`.
- `AgentId::new_placeholder()` or any constructor handing back a magic
  GUID. Return `Result<AgentId, NotConfigured>` or `Option<AgentId>`.
- `format!("agent={agent_uuid}")` where the value is empty and the
  receiver expects an absent value. Guard, or pass `Option`.

## Configurator GUI surfacing

GUIs render any `operator_must_set` GUID field as empty (placeholder
text in the control, not in the value). If an operator types `"0"` or a
magic GUID and clicks Save, the manifest validator (R2) rejects it with
`InvalidValue { reason: "placeholder GUID is not a valid configured
value; leave empty if not yet set" }`, keeping the field highlighted and
the reason in the status pane.

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation:** `let tenant = req.tenant_guid.unwrap_or_else(|| "0".to_string());`
then binding that into an INSERT. A later `WHERE tenant_guid = ?` with
the operator's real GUID misses the row, and a cleanup migration cannot
distinguish "not yet enrolled" from a legitimate zero GUID elsewhere.

**Fix:** keep `Option<Uuid>` end to end and bind it directly — sqlx
binds `None` as SQL `NULL`. The audit log and configurator render an
empty `tenant_guid` when the column is `NULL`, and equality predicates
stop false-matching a placeholder.

